WEBVTT

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:05.970
<i>Everyone is searching for a new world</i>

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:12.070
<i>to attain that overflowing dream.</i>

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:17.650
<i>They all jump over the horizon,</i>

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:26.420
<i>regardless of what lies beyond.</i>

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:34.160
<i>We've run,</i>

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:36.630
<i>we've dived into hope,</i>

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:39.500
<i>and forgotten only courage.</i>

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:44.240
<i>And we've been swept away by the crowd</i>

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:48.900
<i>only to lose something dear to us.</i>

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:54.580
<i>I smile with a twisted face,</i>

00:00:54.580 --> 00:01:01.250
<i>and it was the best smile I could put on.</i>

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:04.630
<i>The inside of my mask overflowed with tears</i>

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:12.270
<i>so I covered my wet mask
with yet another mask.</i>

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:17.170
<i>I continue to walk through
the flat battleground,</i>

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:22.410
<i>and I struggle, unable to warp.</i>

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:32.520
<i>The dream waits quietly on a cape far away.</i>

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:37.260
<i>Even if I fumble around clumsily,</i>

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:41.990
<i>I'm sure I'll still be
able to make it there.</i>

00:01:55.870 --> 00:01:58.600
<i>Takamachi-senpai! See you later!</i>

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:00.590
See ya!

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:15.150
Ow!

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:16.560
Moron!

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:20.250
You're a million years too
early to be sneaking up on me!

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:23.360
Here.

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:24.950
You catch on quick.

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:29.830
Did you hear about how a Hunter

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:31.840
went after Sayoko Shiranagatani?

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:32.840
Yeah...

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:37.080
The Hunters are serious
about coming after us now.

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:40.180
It's not like this is new or anything.

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:42.180
Just don't give them any opportunities.

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:45.380
How long can we keep this up?

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:49.450
Kosuke.

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:52.520
You're not thinking of
anything stupid, are you?

00:02:53.630 --> 00:02:57.460
I've never once thought
of anything stupid.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:10.040
Three weeks until I'm released...

00:03:11.210 --> 00:03:16.240
"Whispering Shadows"

00:03:19.350 --> 00:03:22.920
<i>I hear Rio-san gets out in three weeks,</i>

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:26.190
<i>and it sounds like Sayoko-san
comes back to school tomorrow.</i>

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:29.760
I hope everything stays
nice and quiet like this...

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:32.230
That's completely out of our hands.

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:36.100
<i>But I think that Eyes-san
considered it significant</i>

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:39.170
<i>when you helped with
Sayoko-san's incident.</i>

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:42.370
I didn't necessarily intend to help him.

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:46.400
That might be so from your
point of view, but...

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:48.240
<i>Asazuki-san!</i>

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:50.210
<i>Hello, Hiyoko-chan.</i>

00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:51.840
That's Hiyono!

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:54.810
There's something I wanna ask you today...

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:01.850
The Hunter's characteristics?

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:04.290
Anything at all. Just tell me.

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:06.480
Why not ask Eyes Rutherford?

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:09.720
He's busy at the moment.

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:12.060
Sounds fishy to me...

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:15.200
What does it matter? I just want to know.

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:19.940
What exactly do you want to know
the Hunter's characteristics for?

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:23.740
It's none of your business
what the Blade Children do.

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:26.550
Unfortunately, I have no responsibility
or obligation to tell you.

00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:27.680
What?

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:31.510
I'm sick and tired of being
involved with you all.

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:40.330
Why do you suppose he wanted
to know about the Hunter?

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:41.550
No idea.

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:46.830
In any case, I don't want to
be involved with them anymore.

00:04:46.830 --> 00:04:49.600
You did get involved,
but you couldn't do anything.

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:51.360
That's what you think, isn't it?

00:04:52.370 --> 00:04:57.510
You usually come straight out
with an answer all by yourself.

00:04:57.510 --> 00:05:01.340
It's like giving up before
even saying, "I like you!"

00:05:01.850 --> 00:05:03.750
That's just an example, though...

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:05.280
What's your point?

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:10.590
Everything the Blade Children
have done is unforgivable.

00:05:10.590 --> 00:05:13.960
But they seek redemption.

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:17.200
And they're expecting something from you.

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:19.400
You should try to...

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:20.870
Just drop it.

00:05:27.110 --> 00:05:28.090
Come in!

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:34.240
<i>-Hello, Rio!
-Kanone-kun!</i>

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:39.350
-It's good to see you again.
-It really is!

00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:41.250
These are for you.

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:43.720
Japanese irises are pretty,
don't you think?

00:05:56.270 --> 00:05:59.270
<i>The Hunter who went after
Sayoko Shiranagatani</i>

00:05:59.270 --> 00:06:02.170
<i>was definitely familiar with this area.</i>

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:09.610
<i>Everyone'll be hunted
down if this keeps up.</i>

00:06:21.630 --> 00:06:24.060
<i>I'm not the kind of guy
to quietly sit around</i>

00:06:24.060 --> 00:06:26.630
<i>and wait to be killed!</i>

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:31.500
<i>I need to catch him and get
whatever information I can!</i>

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:34.210
<i>I need to at least figure
out what they're up to...</i>

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:35.400
<i>I need to at least figure
out what they're up to...</i>

00:06:44.620 --> 00:06:48.450
<i>They really spent a lot of
time setting up traps here...</i>

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:00.420
<i>Maybe this was their hideout?</i>

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:08.040
<i>I didn't expect him
to be this anguished!</i>

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:10.410
<i>Has he been marked because he failed?</i>

00:07:10.410 --> 00:07:11.710
<i>Perfect!</i>

00:07:16.150 --> 00:07:18.880
So you get out soon?

00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:19.620
Yeah!

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:22.110
I guess that means I can
return to the front lines!

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:26.290
You intend to fight, Rio?

00:07:26.290 --> 00:07:29.260
I can't wait around to be hunted.

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:38.040
But what lies beyond if you fight?

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:39.940
Using a gun already?!

00:07:39.940 --> 00:07:42.130
He must be really desperate!

00:07:55.690 --> 00:07:57.490
<i>He can't shoot me if I get outside!</i>

00:07:57.490 --> 00:07:58.920
<i>Not with people around!</i>

00:08:02.390 --> 00:08:04.620
<i>Damn! He was expecting me!</i>

00:08:22.050 --> 00:08:23.880
Since childhood, we've been told

00:08:23.880 --> 00:08:28.850
that we bear a cursed fate
from the moment we're born

00:08:28.850 --> 00:08:33.380
and that we mustn't exist.

00:08:34.190 --> 00:08:36.130
And now we garner new sins,

00:08:36.130 --> 00:08:39.460
never once betraying those whispers...

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:43.860
<i>Kanone-kun...</i>

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:51.910
<i>Damn it! How did I get
myself into this?!</i>

00:08:51.910 --> 00:08:54.340
<i>I can forget getting
any information now!</i>

00:09:34.750 --> 00:09:36.310
<i>I can't move!</i>

00:09:40.390 --> 00:09:42.120
Now, of all times...

00:09:43.360 --> 00:09:44.860
Sorry, but I'm...

00:09:44.860 --> 00:09:46.420
What's for lunch today?

00:09:47.430 --> 00:09:51.100
-Are you listening?!
-Yeah, I'm listening!

00:09:52.140 --> 00:09:53.310
Did something happen?

00:09:53.310 --> 00:09:55.370
I'm busy right now. I gotta go.

00:09:55.370 --> 00:09:58.210
Hey! I'm not done talking with you!

00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:01.250
Where are you?

00:10:07.690 --> 00:10:09.350
What are you doing?!

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:14.820
Kosuke...

00:10:21.030 --> 00:10:22.360
Ryoko...

00:10:23.500 --> 00:10:29.200
Buy your own lunch from now on...

00:10:36.980 --> 00:10:38.210
Kosuke...

00:10:42.190 --> 00:10:44.520
The number you are trying to reach is...

00:10:44.520 --> 00:10:47.120
<i>Did something happen to Asazuki-san?</i>

00:10:50.060 --> 00:10:51.560
Oh, it's you.

00:10:51.560 --> 00:10:54.000
That's what I'd like to know.

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:55.930
He's so reckless!

00:10:55.930 --> 00:10:57.300
Reckless?

00:10:57.300 --> 00:11:00.640
Don't tell me something
happened with the Hunters again?

00:11:00.640 --> 00:11:02.110
No idea.

00:11:02.110 --> 00:11:04.740
He doesn't appear to
be on campus, though.

00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:08.740
<i>Narumi-san...</i>

00:11:11.050 --> 00:11:16.720
He won't trouble you.
I'll hold on to his leash.

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:17.790
<i>Takamachi-san!</i>

00:11:17.790 --> 00:11:20.430
What's going on?
This doesn't seem normal!

00:11:20.430 --> 00:11:21.730
Who knows.

00:11:21.730 --> 00:11:24.850
Do you have any ideas
where he might be?!

00:11:25.100 --> 00:11:29.170
No. But I did hear a train,

00:11:29.170 --> 00:11:31.500
so he's probably at some station.

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:34.940
But there are lots of
stations around here!

00:11:34.940 --> 00:11:37.140
Then I'll check them all!

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:42.140
There's really no reason
for you two to worry.

00:11:43.150 --> 00:11:46.020
Yeah. This doesn't have to do with you.

00:11:46.020 --> 00:11:49.890
You shouldn't be involved with us.

00:11:50.190 --> 00:11:51.880
<i>Takamachi-san!</i>

00:11:52.660 --> 00:11:55.790
The hotel that was
blown up the other day.

00:11:55.790 --> 00:11:58.660
Behind it is a freight train depot.

00:12:00.600 --> 00:12:01.860
Thank you.

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:05.600
Do you suppose she'll be
all right by herself?

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:37.030
<i>It's only a matter of
time until he finds me.</i>

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:39.570
<i>Talk about pathetic.</i>

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:42.560
<i>That's what I get for
prowling around by myself.</i>

00:12:43.270 --> 00:12:44.760
<i>Can I run?</i>

00:12:46.850 --> 00:12:49.310
<i>I can still move if I have to, but...</i>

00:12:50.480 --> 00:12:52.580
<i>How long will we keep this up?</i>

00:13:05.860 --> 00:13:10.060
<i>How long will our cursed fate continue?</i>

00:13:10.270 --> 00:13:12.240
That's why we're...

00:13:14.270 --> 00:13:16.840
That was a dumb thing for me to say.

00:13:16.840 --> 00:13:18.880
Forget I said it.

00:13:18.880 --> 00:13:22.880
Rio. I'm truly happy we could meet again.

00:13:22.880 --> 00:13:25.710
I look forward to when you're released.

00:13:31.520 --> 00:13:35.260
<i>I know the weight of the cross we bear.</i>

00:13:35.260 --> 00:13:39.390
<i>And that someday we'll
have to make up for it.</i>

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:47.040
<i>The time of redemption
will come, no matter what.</i>

00:13:49.210 --> 00:13:52.200
<i>I've become a sinner of my own free will.</i>

00:13:53.380 --> 00:13:58.540
<i>Funny how I realize that only now...</i>

00:13:59.150 --> 00:14:00.450
<i>Dammit!</i>

00:14:02.090 --> 00:14:07.860
<i>I guess in the end, I try to
justify things just to live longer...</i>

00:14:13.300 --> 00:14:15.100
<i>I can still move...</i>

00:14:15.100 --> 00:14:21.100
<i>But moving would be an excuse...</i>

00:14:39.220 --> 00:14:40.230
<i>Takamachi-san!</i>

00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:42.560
<i>Have you found Asazuki-san?!</i>

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:44.560
I never expected you to call.

00:14:44.560 --> 00:14:48.590
I haven't found him,
but there's no doubt he's here.

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:50.670
Traps?

00:14:50.670 --> 00:14:51.500
<i>Narumi-san!</i>

00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:54.270
<i>Asazuki-san is being chased by a Hunter!</i>

00:14:54.270 --> 00:14:56.940
It was his decision to chase the Hunter.

00:14:56.940 --> 00:14:58.510
He knew what he was getting into.

00:14:58.510 --> 00:15:01.040
But they're both in serious danger!

00:15:04.280 --> 00:15:05.540
<i>Narumi-san!</i>

00:15:08.750 --> 00:15:10.120
Give me the phone.

00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:14.860
If there are traps,
then it's safe to assume

00:15:14.860 --> 00:15:17.700
that the Hunter has
Asazuki cornered nearby.

00:15:17.700 --> 00:15:19.700
Are there any places to hide?

00:15:19.700 --> 00:15:21.030
Yes.

00:15:21.030 --> 00:15:22.560
Do you see anything else?

00:15:23.840 --> 00:15:26.800
A fuel shed. With lots of oil drums.

00:15:26.910 --> 00:15:30.440
You heard a train on the phone earlier.

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:33.010
Did you hear anything else?

00:15:33.010 --> 00:15:34.550
Anything else?

00:15:34.550 --> 00:15:35.550
Now that you mention it,

00:15:35.550 --> 00:15:37.680
I heard someone running
through a puddle.

00:15:37.680 --> 00:15:39.080
That's a great hint.

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:40.450
I'll look for one.

00:15:41.950 --> 00:15:43.790
Not again.

00:15:43.790 --> 00:15:46.460
What is it? Another trap?

00:15:46.460 --> 00:15:48.730
Yeah.

00:15:48.730 --> 00:15:50.090
Can you disable it?

00:15:50.090 --> 00:15:53.100
Yeah, it's a simple set-up.

00:15:53.100 --> 00:15:55.630
Put it in your pocket after you do.

00:15:55.630 --> 00:15:57.640
You could use it later.

00:15:57.640 --> 00:16:00.430
Understood. I'll call
if anything happens.

00:16:21.430 --> 00:16:27.300
<i>I guess I'll do this
redemption thing heroically.</i>

00:16:34.210 --> 00:16:36.440
Ryoko!

00:16:41.750 --> 00:16:44.210
You're as stupid as ever.

00:16:45.980 --> 00:16:49.110
-Let's go.
-Ryoko. Run.

00:16:49.290 --> 00:16:50.380
You idiot!

00:17:04.070 --> 00:17:05.170
Damn it!

00:17:05.170 --> 00:17:06.400
Wait!

00:17:06.940 --> 00:17:09.340
What are you doing?! Let go!

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:12.640
No.

00:17:12.640 --> 00:17:14.280
Ryoko!

00:17:14.280 --> 00:17:17.680
Promise me you won't kill anymore.

00:17:18.050 --> 00:17:21.880
Promise me you won't kill anyone,
no matter what the reason.

00:17:29.360 --> 00:17:30.930
Are you serious?!

00:17:30.930 --> 00:17:34.200
That's what you want too, isn't it?

00:17:34.200 --> 00:17:35.760
I can tell.

00:17:36.970 --> 00:17:41.210
I came here because I
don't have the heart

00:17:41.210 --> 00:17:43.140
to let you die alone.

00:17:43.140 --> 00:17:45.340
As if I needed your pity.

00:17:51.120 --> 00:17:52.840
Run! Ryoko!

00:17:59.490 --> 00:18:00.580
Kosuke!

00:18:12.040 --> 00:18:14.310
Sounds like he's alive.

00:18:14.310 --> 00:18:16.510
Yeah, somehow.

00:18:16.510 --> 00:18:19.780
But he can't run very far.

00:18:19.780 --> 00:18:22.850
You said there was a
warehouse with oil drums.

00:18:22.850 --> 00:18:24.950
Can you make it there?

00:18:24.950 --> 00:18:27.650
Yeah. But what for?

00:18:27.650 --> 00:18:29.090
Just go.

00:18:55.710 --> 00:18:57.740
Look what you're standing in.

00:19:00.250 --> 00:19:01.740
What is this?!

00:19:03.050 --> 00:19:04.720
Fuel.

00:19:04.720 --> 00:19:06.690
Pull the trigger and we all explode.

00:19:06.690 --> 00:19:08.920
You'll meet your maker, too.

00:19:10.830 --> 00:19:12.820
Two against one.

00:19:14.070 --> 00:19:16.300
The tables have turned.

00:19:27.150 --> 00:19:28.130
Ryoko!

00:19:52.970 --> 00:19:55.370
Salvation and hope...

00:19:55.940 --> 00:20:00.240
Are we honestly fit to seek such things?

00:20:01.550 --> 00:20:03.610
<i>Even Kiyotaka-sama's words</i>

00:20:03.610 --> 00:20:06.520
seem like they were part of a dream now.

00:20:07.320 --> 00:20:10.350
For some reason I'm afraid
to return to the world

00:20:10.350 --> 00:20:12.120
outside this room.

00:20:13.990 --> 00:20:17.130
Yes. In your eyes,
the world outside this room

00:20:17.130 --> 00:20:19.900
might look like Hell.

00:20:19.900 --> 00:20:23.420
But your friends are waiting there.

00:20:31.640 --> 00:20:35.580
<i>Asazuki-san! I'm so glad you're all right!</i>

00:20:38.180 --> 00:20:40.420
<i>Takamachi-san?</i>

00:20:40.420 --> 00:20:42.790
She's just unconscious.

00:20:42.790 --> 00:20:45.860
-All that matters is you're okay.
-Yeah.

00:20:45.860 --> 00:20:51.490
We're still alive, all right...

00:21:05.840 --> 00:21:11.550
<i>A sweet scent washes into my throat</i>

00:21:11.550 --> 00:21:18.250
<i>and my feelings continuously overflow...</i>

00:21:30.370 --> 00:21:36.410
<i>Don't look at me with that same gaze</i>

00:21:36.410 --> 00:21:42.050
<i>that's like you're following a soccer ball.</i>

00:21:42.050 --> 00:21:47.950
<i>I've already grown used to
my third year at the office,</i>

00:21:47.950 --> 00:21:54.530
<i>but did I lose something instead?</i>

00:21:54.530 --> 00:22:00.260
<i>Those days long ago when we
would talk about anything...</i>

00:22:00.260 --> 00:22:05.470
<i>We're finally old enough now</i>

00:22:05.470 --> 00:22:11.310
<i>to have those slightly awkward
discussions about love.</i>

00:22:11.310 --> 00:22:22.920
<i>A single day seems so long,
but a whole year ends so quickly.</i>

00:22:22.920 --> 00:22:28.690
<i>A whole year seems so short,</i>

00:22:28.690 --> 00:22:35.000
<i>but how well will I be able
to live the rest of my life?</i>

00:22:39.090 --> 00:22:41.160
Time for Hiyono's Useful News Report!

00:22:41.160 --> 00:22:44.830
Things waver when you're dizzy,
and they waver when it's hot out!

00:22:44.830 --> 00:22:46.660
They say fire can't put fire out,

00:22:46.660 --> 00:22:48.570
but you can fight fire with fire,

00:22:48.570 --> 00:22:50.570
plus fire's no match for water!

00:22:50.570 --> 00:22:52.770
<i>Next episode's highlight is
Hiyono-chan and Narumi-san</i>

00:22:52.770 --> 00:22:55.210
doing a bucket relay!

00:22:55.210 --> 00:22:57.640
On the next Spiral: Bond of Reasoning...

00:22:57.640 --> 00:22:59.340
The Sound of a Heart Breaking

00:22:59.340 --> 00:23:03.880
Don't fall into water while
trying to avoid the fire!

00:23:03.880 --> 00:23:06.210
That's all for today's Hiyono's Playhouse!
